at it was a  desert of sorts there was nothing there  so if there's nothing to eat when they  arrive could great whites be stocking up  on pinnipeds before the journey in order  to sustain themselves white sharks want  the easy meal so they're gonna go to a  place where there's a lot of seals and  sea lions a place like the California  coast  so our humans here simply in the middle  of a feeding frenzy is that what's  causing this alarming spike in attacks  according to Nosal the answer lies far  below the surface of the cafe where in  2018 scientists make an unexpected  finding involving the very thing that  appeared to be absent food turns out  that there's actually a lot living there  there's all kinds of fish and crabs and  things in the water there  this prey just lives much deeper than  could previously be seen on satellite  images so because they're feeding there  I don't think the white shark stocking  up on food right before their migration  is a sound explanation for the uptick in  shark bites something else must be  driving great whites to attack and maybe  it isn't what they're hunting but what's  under them  [Music]
 

